  "utmEpsg": 32616,
  "placementWhy": "Scale bar (60 m = 424 px, 0.1415 m/px; the survey's own penetrations agree: cenote de los franceses to the airspace, 111 m = 780 px drawn, 0.142 m/px; the north end to the airspace, 135 m = 921 px, 0.147 m/px), north at 18.2 deg left of up, shifted onto eight points of the caleta and coast (surface features after Andrews 1975, matched on the Mapbox satellite and OSM's coastline/water): the channel's north-east and north-west corners, two points along the channel, the peninsula tip, the mouth's west point, the cove corner east of the point, the north end of the bay west of the mouth. Rotation and shift fitted by least squares at the bar's scale: residuals 1.6-9.0 m (RMS 5.7 m; worst the mouth's west point 9.0 m and the cove corner 8.7 m, both pulled in because the surface is drawn larger). The 18.2 deg rotation is 4.6 deg more than the north arrow (13.6 deg left of up): plausibly a magnetic arrow, the 1979 declination being a few degrees east (not checked). A free similarity fit on the same eight points fits them better (RMS 3.9 m, max 5.4 m) but at 0.158 m/px, 12% larger than the cave's scale bar and its written penetrations: the surface was redrawn at its own scale onto the survey, so the cave's scale rules (a free fit would stretch the cave by 12%, about 35 m at its north end). Checks, not fitted: the little bay in the caleta's east wall near the mouth (7.1 m off, where the footbridge lands today) and the tip of the north arm (17.7 m: on the satellite the arm is a dark channel under the trees, OSM water, running due north while the map draws it bending north-east). The west arm and the north-west lobe fall on land and canopy now (filled or hidden). Compared with the previous placement (scale bar, north arrow -13.6 deg, three points): the caleta moves 2 m, cenote de los franceses 9 m, the airspace 13 m, cenote de Felipe 18 m, the north end 25 m. Compared with the unverified Beddows 2003 sketch (x-caret.json): not re-checked here (being reworked separately). Reviewed on the satellite by the user (2026-10-02) and accepted: no longer unverified (it was: No cenote of the map has a position in the database (the Xcaret sistema's only cave has neither name nor coordinates), and none of its cenotes or its open Xcaret airspace shows on the satellite (park buildings and canopy now). Placed only by the surface features the map copies from Andrews 1975 - th).",
